# Neduco Project Rules

## Architecture

**Feature-Sliced Design (FSD)**
- Strict separation of layers: `app`, `pages`, `widgets`, `features`, `entities`, `shared`
- No cross-imports inside the same layer slicing
- Respect FSD boundaries: lower layers can import from higher layers, but never the reverse
- Example: `pages` can import from `widgets`, `features`, `entities`, `shared`; `shared` cannot import from any other layer

## Styling Code Style

**CSS Modules**
- Local component styles MUST use CSS Modules with strict camelCase selectors
- Correct: `.metricCard`, `.pageLayoutHeader`, `appSidebarLink`
- Incorrect: `.metric-card`, `.page-layout__header`, `app-sidebar__link` (kebab-case/BEM banned in modules)
- TSX must reference module classes: `className={styles.metricCard}`

**Global Utilities**
- Systemic global helper utilities are hosted ONLY in `src/app/styles/index.css`
- Examples: `.dashboard-grid`, `.detail-grid`, `.metric-card`
- These can be used as global string literals in TSX: `className="dashboard-grid"`
- Do not duplicate global utilities in CSS modules

## Localization (i18n)

**Page-Specific Translations**
- Page-specific translations must be modularized and co-located within the page directory
- Structure: `src/pages/[name]/i18n/ru.ts`, `src/pages/[name]/i18n/en.ts`, `src/pages/[name]/i18n/uz.ts`
- Export format: `export const pageName = { 'page.key': 'Translation', ... }`

**Central Registry**
- The central registry `src/shared/i18n/translations.ts` imports and spreads these local dictionary modules dynamically
- Import pattern:
  ```ts
  import { dashboard as dashboardRu } from '../../pages/dashboard/i18n/ru';
  import { dashboard as dashboardEn } from '../../pages/dashboard/i18n/en';
  import { dashboard as dashboardUz } from '../../pages/dashboard/i18n/uz';
  ```
- Merge pattern:
  ```ts
  export const translations = {
    ru: { ...dashboardRu, ...loginRu, ...profileRu, /* ... */ },
    en: { ...dashboardEn, ...loginEn, ...profileEn, /* ... */ },
    uz: { ...dashboardUz, ...loginUz, ...profileUz, /* ... */ },
  };
  ```
- Do not hardcode page keys directly into the global monolith block

## Coding Principles

- Prefer architectural consistency over quick and dirty inline overrides
- Follow established patterns rather than creating exceptions
- Maintain clear separation of concerns across layers
- When refactoring, update both TSX and CSS Module files to stay in sync
- Use TypeScript strictly - no `any` types unless absolutely necessary
- Keep components focused and single-responsibility
